    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_first_degree_core_one_quadratic_gap_four_double_root_heavy_quotient_cubic_residual",
    "title": "A=1 quadratic separated double-root heavy-quotient cubic residual",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "exact D1 divisibility and type [2] on the separated correction locus",
    "statement": "Assume the double-root correction form S_B is squarefree and coprime to the supported factor g_*. Divide Q(t,X)-Q(t,x_*) by X-x_*. The contracted Pade value at x_* and every moment of this quotient are divisible by D_1=g_*S_B^2; after division they form a degree-at-most-three vector satisfying an exact Hankel recurrence. Each of the two correction roots has exactly one positive regular Smith invariant, of exponent two. Nonreduced and shared corrections remain outside the claim.",
